{
  "schema": 1,
  "source_parent": "59f2b5eeb8cd461e93fa63f1fa49493231c01818",
  "problem": "The Native world snapshot has its canonical sparse coordinates but an empty appearance until graphics_draw_hybrid publishes the completed scene. Constructing the indexed coordinates adapter earlier validates the empty grid, rejects its scene and returns-1 for every substrate neighbour. Vertical terrain then keeps the generic floor/dirt fallback even when a compatible visible floor is beside it.",
  "change": "Move the existing visible-neighbour substrate pass into the already copied static-detail include. Use the canonical sparse XYZ adapter before appearance is bound, and reuse the already-owned string for the selected copy. No Native map read or permission changes.",
